jures images of the red  and blue pill from the matrix and alice  in wonderland in which one pill reveals  the true world while the other leaves  you in ignorant bliss kind of like how  our innies have no idea what happens in  the outside world and vice versa the  other color that's prevalent throughout  the season is green the office is  covered in it green is often used as a  color to represent sickness so a fitting  choice for our severed macro refinement  team green also happens to be one of two  colors in jane egan's first prototype  for the chip used in the severance  process the other color being blue blue  and green also happened to be the color  of helly's dress of the gala as well as  her earrings in episode 1 we learned  that miss casey also known as mark's  wife was an educator who taught russian  literature mark was a history professor  so it could be that they were colleagues  at the nearby college where mark worked  and that's where they fell in love it's  also kind of ironic that mark was a  history teacher yet spends much of the  season not remembering who he is the  majority of mark and casey's  interactions happen during quote-unquote  wellness meetings where two very  interesting objects are introduced one  is the red green candle that miss cobell  stole from mark's basement from a bin  labelled gemma's crafts gemma being the  real name of miss casey i think cobell  is secretly trying to see if this might  spark either of them recognizing the  other we also see mark mold out of clay  at tree the thing gemma supposedly  crashed her car into and died when mark  leaves work on helly's first day we see  her audi holding a bouquet of flowers in  episode 2 we'll see these are from seth  milchik in honor of her first day of  work miss cobell gives two contradictory  statements about her mother one in the  office where she tells mark that her  mother was an atheist and one in the  outside world where she tells mark that  her mother was a devout catholic 