n  who is mentioned as being the black  sheep of the family jane refers to  someone known as the grandfather and i  think he's referring to kier the name  cure derives from gaelic meaning the  dark one we'll later get a glimpse of  mark and irving's license plates which  are colored black and emblazoned with  the latin phrase remedium hominibus  which translates to a cure given to  mankind remember that lumen did start  off as a medical company in episode 3  miss casey says of irving's audi that he  likes the sound of radar which is the  name of his dog and later in episode 8  she tells mark in his wellness meeting  that she's only been up for combined 107  hours and that eight hours she spent  looking after hely was the longest she  hasn't been asleep to me this suggests  that her other self could be in some  sort of coma you may have noticed that  much of the lumens severed workspace is  empty almost as if they are expecting  more workers marx audi even remarks that  the company homes of which he lives in  one are relatively empty when combined  with james remark that he wants everyone  in the world to be chipped it leads me  to believe lumen will be expanding its  workforce but first they need to get  over some political hurdles hence helena  egan's connection to senator arteta the  name of the birthing retreat devin  attends is called damona who was a  goddess worshiped in gaul whose name  roughly translates to divine cow kind of  weird in episode 5 we see this painting  called the courtship of kier and imogen  who fell in love while working together  at an ether factory as you do with  helena being an egan and her innie  establishing a romantic connection with  her work partner mark i can't help but  see the parallels here the name of the  restaurant markets a gift card to is  pip's diner named after one of lumen's  past ceos when irving says goodbye to  hallie and mark before their big plan he  says the line okay kids  let's find out what's for dinner which  is what he was chastised for saying in  episode one hi kids what's for dinner  during the weird waffle dance dillon  uncovers this cat of nine tails whip the  same one keir holds in the painting of  the taming of the tempers each of the  tails represents one of keir's nine  virtues all those pitchers milkshake  took throughout the season were all part  of helena's publicity stunt to garner  favor for lumen and the severance  process you may have also noticed the  technology at lumen is pretty outdated  this serves many purposes for example it  makes it so that their work is protected  from conventional hacking methods and  this type of nostalgia may make the  workers more at ease with their office  life it also creates a stark  juxtaposition to the outside world which  has things like smartphones and is set  in and around 2020 as evidenced by  mark's driver's license the lumen  handbook we see in episode 2 can  actually be downloaded for free as part  of severnce's companion book the  lexington letters to which i'll leave a  link to in the description below for  achieving 100 on a particular file the  prize is a caricature and this one is of  dylan in a muscle show which he thinks  is audi competes in when mark walks  after his date with devin's doula  there's a sign in the background that  reads we sell severance compatible  attire which i think is just great  attention to detail this statue of cure  where two members of the whole mine  collective protest is in front of the  hall of records which is pretty ironic  since the whole act of severance is  about not remembering i love this  framing here where pd's head is  imprisoned reflecting his mental state  there are certain characters that wear  this lumen water drop pin these include  the secretary at the front of lumen  natalie the pr lady and miss casey do  they have something in common i.e never  leave lumen or is this just a  coincidence in episode 3 there's a sign  that clearly states not to sit on keir  egan's bed but dylan is explicitly told  to after his waffle party cobell's  bedroom looks almost like a prison drab  concrete walls minimally furnished with  a hospital-like bed her shrine has some  interesting bits of information like a  photo of what is likely her as a child  attending the myrtle eagan school for  girls perhaps this is where she wound up  after her mother passed in episode 6  mark goes on another date at a  restaurant called gerhart's another  eagan ceo in the security room we can  see there are dozens of severed workers  at least in this specific section of  lumen there could be other sections here  plus we know according to the lexington  letters that there are other lumen  branches that also engage in severance  i've also noticed that the state  abbreviation used throughout the season  is pe and i'm not american but as far as  i know there is no state with that  abbreviation it makes me wonder if we're  in some sort of alternate reality but  here is where i leave it to you i'm sure  i missed a bunch of stuff and if you  haven't seen my other ending explain  video be sure to check it out i've left  a link to it in the description below  thanks for watching everyone for more  bad takes you can follow me on twitter  and instagram at thingstoryt and until  next time remember  who are you  you

